== is it the conv or the pad? ==
conv2d groups=3, no pad                                      identical
conv2d groups=3, built-in padding=2 (zeros)                  identical
conv2d groups=3, stride 2, no pad                            identical
conv2d groups=3 + tf.pad constant                            identical
conv2d groups=3 + tf.pad circular                            identical
conv2d groups=3 + tf.pad reflect                             DIFFERS 29/29, 5.4e-07
conv2d groups=3 + tf.pad replicate                           DIFFERS 29/29, 1.1e-06
== tf.pad alone, by width (a border pixel gets width+1 adds) ==
tf.pad replicate width 1                                     DIFFERS 29/29, 5.9e-07
tf.pad replicate width 2                                     DIFFERS 29/29, 2.4e-06
tf.pad replicate width 4                                     DIFFERS 29/29, 2.9e-06
tf.pad replicate width 16                                    DIFFERS 29/29, 3.6e-05
tf.pad reflect width 1                                       DIFFERS 29/29, 3.7e-07
tf.pad reflect width 2                                       DIFFERS 29/29, 5.9e-07
tf.pad reflect width 4                                       DIFFERS 29/29, 1.2e-06
tf.pad reflect width 16                                      DIFFERS 29/29, 1.1e-06
== reflect and replicate through advanced indexing ==
advanced index pad replicate width 2                         identical
advanced index pad replicate width 16                        identical
advanced index pad reflect width 2                           identical
advanced index pad reflect width 16                          identical
conv2d + advanced index reflect pad                          identical
gaussian blur as W @ x @ W.T                                 identical
